    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d808">

                <pb facs="1570" n="1530" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1530"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/4–2154: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 808<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the
                        Secretary of State, at Paris</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d808-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-23T15:04:00-05:00">April 23, 1954—3:04
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tosec 8. We agree with British suggestions as set forth London’s 636 to
                        Paris<anchor n="2" xml:id="d808-f2"/> for separate approaches to Jordan and
                    Israel by tripartite powers and with proposed tactics. In face of Soviet
                    obstructionism and Arab opposition to meeting between parties, we also are not
                    sanguine as to constructive results from SC proceedings. However since we still
                    exploring what may be done in SC we believe we should postpone decision on
                    timing of approach until course SC discussions becomes clearer. In interim three
                    powers could usefully clarify among themselves their views on concrete measures
                    which might be taken and on terms in which approach to Jordan and Israel should
                    be made.</p>
                <p>If you concur you may wish to discuss with Eden and Bidault along above
                    lines.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d808-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d808-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to London, Tel Aviv, and Amman.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d808-f2" n="2" xml:id="d808-f2-content">
